{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings","id":1037706,"title":"[2E] Multilimb beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-25T01:23:11-08:00","id":1037706,"title":"[2E] Multilimb beings","content":"I want to place in story Life Archmaster that looks like this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/EBOfBJD.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>What would be rules for beings having more hands than normal - still no extra actions in one turn?</b> And just because I'm curious - What level of Life would be needed for next working pair of limbs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T01:52:22-08:00","id":1037710,"title":"","content":"No extra actions. Just give them an equipment bonus to actions, or in case of attacks, decrease their opponents Defense as if they were attacked by multiple attackers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T02:03:12-08:00","id":1037713,"title":"","content":"Refer to the Demon Form ability 'Extra Mechanical Limbs'.<br /> <br /> Patterning should be enough to grow them. Maybe even Weaving.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T02:24:46-08:00","id":1037719,"title":"","content":"Weaving/Perfecting should be enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Patterning</b> spells allow a mage to <b>completely transform a<br /> target</b> into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s<br /> purview. A memory can be replaced wholesale (Mind),<br /> the mage can turn herself (or a target) into an animal<br /> (Life), or she can teleport by \u201crewriting\u201d her own location<br /> (Space). </div> </div> </div>And this is far from complete transformation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T03:37:31-08:00","id":1037742,"title":"","content":"Oh, an idea - could mutiple limbs somehow affect using mudras? I visualize some mudras being based on hand signs (common in Buddhism), and having many hands could potentially help with that. Maybe OP, but this is an archmage we're talking about anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T03:53:11-08:00","id":1037752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037742#post1037742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, an idea - could mutiple limbs somehow affect using mudras? I visualize some mudras being based on hand signs (common in Buddhism), and having many hands could potentially help with that. Maybe OP, but this is an archmage we're talking about anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was thinking the same - like using multiple Tools ( those in the picture ), each in other hand, each one adding to the same turn of spellcasting - +4 bonus on the first turn from four Tools... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T04:00:07-08:00","id":1037756,"title":"","content":"Or you could not break the system and use it as a way of activating Persona Tool Yantra, because this dude probably incorporated the arms into their Shadow Name. Yantra system balance is really frail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T04:05:15-08:00","id":1037759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037756#post1037756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you could not break the system and use it as a way of activating Persona Tool Yantra, because this dude probably incorporated the arms into their Shadow Name. Yantra system balance is really frail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, but I like smashing systems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, using it as a persona Yantra seems the most acceptable within the existing system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T04:41:26-08:00","id":1037765,"title":"","content":"Spells and their powers are restricted by size of your pool. Yantra System is designed in such way that your spells are most powerful when you have time to incorporate multiple Yantras into the spell. Incovenience of doing so in combat (and combat tends to be over in 2, 3, maybe 4 rounds at most) is a real balancing attempt and keeping power of Mages in check - smaller pools mean less dice to throw at Potency means less firepower and smaller chance of piercing Withstands.<br /> This is also why having access to big, one-shot Yantra is such a big deal for combat Mages - most Yantras are +1 on their own. This means that having an access to Mudra or possessing combat-applicable Shadow Name is a great deal, as it can literally triple your Yantra output. Casting a spell multiple turns is rarely a good choice; often, it's better to try twice in a row rather than to try incorporating multiple yantras into one casting.<br /> <br /> Basically, Mage in combat (or any other sequence where you operate in turns) has following choice of Yantras:<br /> - Tool Yantra with +1 bonus<br /> - Shadow Name, anywhere between 1 and 4 (need merit)<br /> - Mudra, anywhere between 1 and 5 (need Rote and Skill investment)<br /> - Dedicated Tool, with +1 bonus and -2 Paradox<br /> - High Speech, with +2 bonus and drawback of being time consuming<br /> You pick one and get it done. Usually you will pick either a Mudra or Shadow Name if you need factors, and Dedicated Tool if you need Reach. Don't underestimate Dedicated Tools! Especially for lower-gnosis characters! -2 Paradox for them is, effectively, 2 Free Reach.<br /> <br /> &quot;But WHW, why ability to add up to 4 +1 Yantras in single turn matters if you could do the same by adding a single big Yantra?&quot;, you might ask. Well, it matters because this effectively gives you +4 to instant casting without investing in Shadow Name/Rotes (though I'm going to say that cost of extra arms might counter that), but more importantly, you can grab 1 Dedicated Tool and 3 Soul Stones, giving you anything between +4 Yantra Bonus and -8 Paradox if Soul Stones are yours,(so about 4 Reach at the level this happens) and +10 Yantra Bonus and -2 Paradox, if they are another Mages of higher Gnosis than you.<br /> This sounds little too good for Life 3 effect, don't you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-25-2017, 07:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:34:28-08:00","id":1037779,"title":"","content":"I agree with @whw in this case, yantra system is fragile. <br /> Little digresion though. Wouldn't it be waste and weird if Arcanum governing magic couldn't apply penalty or boost to casting rolls? We go with a Prime spell that boosts Yantra by potency (up to five) and every Yantra affected costs 1 mana.<br /> So while Life could change things like speaking fast for High Speech to be reflexive - Prime, Mind and maybe Time could speed you up more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:37:53-08:00","id":1037780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037719#post1037719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weaving/Perfecting should be enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And this is far from complete transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you perhaps saying this isn't even our final form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:47:20-08:00","id":1037784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037780#post1037780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you perhaps saying this isn't even our final form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely xD Pack some sweet Reach and Potency into Transform Life and unleash your six winged, four armed Archangel fury upon thee!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:56:20-08:00","id":1037788,"title":"","content":"Last time we tried that Mages got all jelly and called us Left Handed. No love for Echo Walkers!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037779#post1037779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with @whw in this case, yantra system is fragile.<br /> Little digresion though. Wouldn't it be waste and weird if Arcanum governing magic couldn't apply penalty or boost to casting rolls? We go with a Prime spell that boosts Yantra by potency (up to five) and every Yantra affected costs 1 mana.<br /> So while Life could change things like speaking fast for High Speech to be reflexive - Prime, Mind and maybe Time could speed you up more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but there are other ways to represent &quot;boosting power of magic&quot; than applying +/- to Yantras. 9, 8 Again and Rote Qualities are the first things that come to mind, as they modify power of your spell (first two directly increase your chance of Exceptional Success, working pretty well to represent POWER OVERWHELMING aspect of AWESOME MASTERY OF PURE MAGIC, while Rote Quality does that + boosts your baseline chance of success), and more importantly, they don't push the limit on your factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-25-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:47:11-08:00","id":1037806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037788#post1037788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last time we tried that Mages got all jelly and called us Left Handed. No love for Echo Walkers!<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, but there are other ways to represent &quot;boosting power of magic&quot; than applying +/- to Yantras. 9, 8 Again and Rote Qualities are the first things that come to mind, as they modify power of your spell (first two directly increase your chance of Exceptional Success, working pretty well to represent POWER OVERWHELMING aspect of AWESOME MASTERY OF PURE MAGIC, while Rote Quality does that + boosts your baseline chance of success), and more importantly, they don't push the limit on your factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that. Weirdly, it doesn't change much in combat. You are still limited to one Yantra per turn so your gain on any Yantra is 3-4 dice. That's one or two steps in potency. But mostly spend on narrative effects like duration(Cow benefits with one or two dice), and scale .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:32:54-08:00","id":1037933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1037706-2e-multilimb-beings?p=1037713#post1037713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refer to the Demon Form ability 'Extra Mechanical Limbs'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking over from <b>Demon</b>'s text:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD, p. 206</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Extra Mechanical Limbs</b><br /> The God-Machine creates multi-limbed angels to build or repair bits of Infrastructure as having multiple limbs on one angel is better than creating multiple angels for the same job. Those demons that keep these aspects, or choose to manifest them, find the use of additional arms useful in destroying those same bits of Infrastructure. They are also very useful in a combat.<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> An extra set of fully functional mechanical arms constructed of metal and plastics protrude from the demon\u2019s torso. The demon controls these limbs separately from his normal arms, but they work flawlessly in tandem with his other limbs.<br /> <b>System: </b>The demon can use his mechanical arms to hold additional items or to assist in anything else he is doing that requires hands. For example, he can hold a shield and a two-handed weapon and still have an extra hand free for other activities. If the demon uses all of his arms towards one endeavor, such as swinging a large sword, grappling an opponent, or climbing a sheer surface, he gains a +3 bonus to his Strength. Extra limbs can also help the demon defend himself against an attack. If the demon has at least two unarmed hands, he gains a +3 bonus to his Defense. Since the arms are made out of metal, they deal lethal damage instead of bashing if used for an unarmed attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Last sentence do not apply to our Archmage idea, but it seems he will be combat monster, with bonus to Strength actions and Defense, being also Life mage himself... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}